Fixed. The bug was in `src/url_utils.ts:11-16`: the loop over `TRACKING_PARAMS` had a `break` after deleting the first match, so only one tracking param ever came out. Since `URLSearchParams.delete()` is a no-op for absent keys, the fix is just to drop the `has` guard and the `break`:

```
  for (const param of TRACKING_PARAMS) {
    u.searchParams.delete(param);
  }
```

Verified in the disposable run root: `deno test` passes 7/7, including 4 new cases in `tests/url_utils.test.ts` covering the reported `utm_source`+`fbclid` case, all four params at once (with a non-tracking `id` kept), single-param, and no-param URLs (including the trailing-slash drop on `https://example.com/`). No changes to any files outside the run root.


